{"type":"standard","title":"Kelly Ayotte","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Kelly Ayotte</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q22354","titles":{"canonical":"Kelly_Ayotte","normalized":"Kelly Ayotte","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Kelly Ayotte</span></span>"},"pageid":6538022,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9b/Gov._Kelly_Ayotte.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":227,"height":340},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9b/Gov._Kelly_Ayotte.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":227,"height":340},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1377205944","tid":"6e55fee9-bb16-11f1-b042-5c52a64c4403","timestamp":"2026-09-28T08:27:24Z","description":"Governor of New Hampshire since 2025","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kelly_Ayotte","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kelly_Ayotte?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kelly_Ayotte?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Kelly_Ayotte"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kelly_Ayotte","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Kelly_Ayotte","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kelly_Ayotte?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Kelly_Ayotte"}},"extract":"Kelly Ann Ayotte is an American attorney and politician serving since 2025 as the 83rd governor of New Hampshire. A member of the Republican Party, she served from 2011 to 2017 as a United States senator from New Hampshire and from 2004 to 2009 as the 27th attorney general of New Hampshire.","extract_html":"<p><b>Kelly Ann Ayotte</b> is an American attorney and politician serving since 2025 as the 83rd governor of New Hampshire. A member of the Republican Party, she served from 2011 to 2017 as a United States senator from New Hampshire and from 2004 to 2009 as the 27th attorney general of New Hampshire.</p>"}